==Strategy==
A very difficult stage with an introduction to powerful [[Surge Attack]]s, your main goal is to prevent Kappy Jr. from setting off as many Surges as possible by making him miss frequently. Using almost any meatshield that is not immune to Surges is actively '''harmful''', as it'll just make Kappy Jr. attack more and act as stepping stones for him to create Surges. Thankfully, his foreswing is long enough and his range is rather short to where many conventional midrangers like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] can outrange him safely, and he gets knocked back frequently enough to not stand ground easily. Try to apply crowd-control effects to Kappy Jr. to prevent him from pushing hard, and take advantage of the Scissoroos to make them knock back your attackers, making Kappy Jr. miss even more frequently. If one has powerful [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune units]], such as certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]], however, the stage becomes much more trivial since they wouldn't be harmed by Kappy Jr's powerful Surges and beat him and the peons from there. If at a decent level (10+),  Thunderbolt cannon is reccomended here, as it can allow slime to get free damage without risking surges. Breakerblast can also be helpful to recover ground.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
The following units are either required to beat this stage, or are massively helpful for subduing Kappy Jr.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: Requires high level and Survive [[Talents|Talent]], '''minimum level 40'''. Cameraman is your main ranged meatshield against Kappy Jr. Maxing the Survive Talent guarantees that she will endure an attack from Kappy Jr. or a Scissoroo. Without these high levels and Talents on Cameraman, don't even try this stage.
*Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]: With his Surge Immunity Talent, Li'l King Dragon becomes one of the best units here. He has amazing range and attack, and can stack easily. Just beware of his cost and Single Attack.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Your secondary attack force right alongside Cameraman. His unnaturally high health lets him survive attacks from Kappy Jr. Upgrading him to level 40 or more is ideal to have the best chances at winning. Talents such as Attack Buff and [[Wave Attack]] are very well useful.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Because Boulder Cat despawns moments after it attacks, it can easily cause Kappy Jr. to miss his attack and prevent his surge from even appearing. For it to work, though, you need some Research [[Cat Combo|Combos]] equating to one L Combo, and ensure your top priority is to have Boulder Cat deployed as soon as its recharge ends so it can consistently stall Kappy Jr. This is the most consistent way to stall Kappy Jr. easily for any player, though it requires having to beat [[An Ancient Curse]] first to be able to access the [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|stage]] it's obtained from and some timing practice.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]]: '''If you don't have his [[True Form]], don't use him.''' Without the knockback effect, Kappy Jr. will still get an attack off and destroy anything non-Surge immune. Use Macho Crystal Cat sparingly and with careful timing, as if he misses, then you are most likely screwed.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]]: His True Form is nigh-required, as the extra freeze duration is mandatory for chain-knockbacking Kappy Jr. and keeping him in check. Use him like a secondary or backup Macho Crystal Cat. Obtaining the True Form at this point isn't that difficult as the [[Revenge of the Dreamer (Merciless)|stage]] it's obtained from is comparatively easy for most players trying to clear this stage.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Not a must-pick like the previous Cats, but can be useful. Maxed Slow Talent is required for him to make an impact and be worth the money, and Survive Talent is great since Kappy Jr. pushes hard. Use him if you have an extra slot and you don't have any helpful Ubers.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: If one lacks Boulder Cat and/or wishes to do the stage without it, this unit is VERY amazing at stalling Kappy Jr. especially when paired with Cyberpunk, as Deadeye's Slow+Knockback prevents Kappy Jr. from pushing very easily, coupled with long range keeping him safe. Just make sure to get rid of the peons quick, as his Single Target inhibits him from easily stalling him, especially when The Thrillerz protect Kappy Jr.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]]: With Talents, Gato Amigo becomes the most accessible Surge-Immune meatshield at this point barring [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]]. His spammability, slow speed creating small gaps and low price will make Kappy Jr. have a hard time pushing. '''ONLY''' bring him if you're bringing other Surge-immune attackers, as if you are bringing units that are not immune to Surges, there is almost no point as they'll get Surged to death.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]: Jagando is a midranger that's Strong Against Traitless, with a 100% Knockback Effect/Level 1 Surge on his third hit, on top of being Surge Immune himself. This makes him a great choice for stalling Kappy Jr. as the repeated Knockback effects (the Surge is usually able to hit him again for a second Knockback) will constantly interrupt his attacks and reduce the amount of Surges he may spawn.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]]: Despite of being neither Surge-immune nor Resistant to Alien, Doguemon's base HP is high enough to hold the fort while Jagando is on downtime. Alternatively, if boosted enough, he could be used simutanously with Jagando to completely stall Kappy Jr. and make the most out of each Jagando cycle. This strategy can effectively trivialize the Special only Mission.
*Most [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Cats with Surge Immunity]]: Despite your best efforts, Kappy Jr. is still likely to get a Surge off every now and again. These units help to minimize the resulting catastrophic consequences.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Not many [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] work at all in this stage simply due to Kappy's Surges and DPS, but there are few that can be of great assistance.
*[[Myrcia (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Myrcia ξ]]: She has a Surge Immunity Talent and can Dodge [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless Enemies]], which makes her a decent pick for this stage. Her Wave Attack can hit the Scissoroos for extra damage.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: A prohibitively expensive midranger with a steep True Form cost, Lasvoss has somewhat fast cooldown for an Uber, is Immune to Surges and can potentially deal extreme amounts of damage with his 50% Strengthen at 30% Health and 30% Savage Blows, alongside a 100% chance to Survive a Lethal Strike. They aren't consistent, but yield great results with a well-placed hit.
*[[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Anubis]]: Only good if you have his Immune to Surge Talent, but this stage starves you of cash, so unless you have no other options, don't waste your NP.
*[[Kenshin Himura (Uber Rare Cat)|Kenshin Himura CC]]: With Surge Immunity, anti-Traitless capability, high range and decent damage against everything else, his kit makes him a powerful unit to bring to this stage.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: Though not immune to Surges, their mighty Waves can cripple the Scissoroos and deal considerable damage to Kappy Jr., even if they only get in one attack. Upgrading them to level 40 is highly recommended, as they are highly valuable even outside of this stage. Do note that they only outrange Kappy by 10, which is a VERY small range gap.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: Can deal great damage to Kappy Jr. and his Omni Strike can chip the Scissoroos, with Surge Immunity to top it off.
*Any [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusive will do well. Most are anti-Traitless specialists that are too good to ignore despite lacking Surge immunity. [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]], [[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Lady of Mourning]], [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] and the [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cat]] [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]] in particular actually have it, greatly improving their survivability on top of their already amazing abilities.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]]: An excellent crowd-controller vs. every enemy here with good tanking capabilities.
*[[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Rex]]: Its Surge Immunity and high range can help chip away at Kappy Jr. and clean up the peons with its Explosions.

