'''Difficulty:''' ★★★☆☆

'''Battle:''' Start the stage by spamming Catellites and Mohawk Cats, eventually upgrading your wallet to level 5. As soon as your cats are about to trigger the boss wave, don't spawn anything until the Scissoroos are about to reach the Cat Base. Send out Green Shell Cat to narrowly intercept them and then immediately follow that up with Awakened Bahamut Cat—and Thunderbolt as Kappy Jr. is about to attack. Spawn Neo Driller Cat to Weaken him as everything gets knocked back by the initial explosion. This gives Bahamut the opportunity to survive for all 5 rebound opportunities, thus allowing you to chain Kappy alongside Idi:N2 and Neo Cutter Cat. However, <u>'''only send out Idi and Cutter when absolutely necessary to continue the chain.'''</u> They have a massive tendency to rush in at inopportune times if used haphazardly!

Every attempt following this lineup varies immensely, but a rule of thumb to keep in mind is to never allow Kappy Jr. to advance too far after taking a damage knockback. If he manages to slip his way into Driller's blind spot and get an attack off, the run is dead then and there. These are the moments to look out for when deploying Idi and Cutter, as they can distract/knock back Kappy Jr. and bail you out of a tricky situation. After the chain, you can either destroy the enemy base if Bahamut survives, or stall out the enemies until your rushers recharge.

