'''Difficulty:''' ★★★☆☆

'''Battle:''' Stall the Scissoroo until you're able to afford Jagando Jr., then start upgrading your wallet before stacking Macho Leg Cats and Manic Macho Leg Cats. Your main priority is to defend Jagando Jr. as well as you possibly can; he is by all means the hard-carry here, dealing good damage to everybody and reliably crowd-controlling the boss. There's surprisingly a lot of room for error thanks to his relatively quick recharge rate. You can usually get another Jagando Jr. out by the time the previous one dies, unless you mess up catastrophically. Manic Island Cat and Macho Leg Cat are used for clearing out The Thrillerz that tend to distract Jagando Jr. and cause him to miss. As long as you can get into a good rhythm, this clear should be a walk in the park.

