'''Difficulty:''' ★★★★☆

'''Battle:''' A variation of the classic Boulder Cat strategy that takes advantage of Kappy Jr.'s backswing animation to hold him in place in a Sisyphean manner. It is recommended to review Kartoffel's walkthrough below, as words alone cannot describe the procedure nearly as well as said video.

Use Li'l Mohawk to stall for cash at the beginning, then start stacking Cameraman Cats and Pizza Cats. They're both very slow, which means it'll take them a while to reach the enemy base. That downtime allows your Cameraman stack to build up to epic proportions, helping take care of the two Scissoroos that spawn with Kappy Jr. Look for an opportunity to time a Boulder Cat such that it causes Kappy Jr. to initiate an attack, but vanishes just before Kappy Jr. finishes his foreswing animation. This usually leads to him missing entirely all the while your midranges continue to pummel him to death. At this point, get into the cycle of spawning Boulder Cats at roughly a 2.5-second interval to keep Kappy Jr. in said loop. Cyberpunk Cat further aids this strategy by being an additional layer of crowd-control who even targets the Scissoroos. Keep this up until Kappy Jr. eventually dies, and be careful not to mess up your Boulder Cat timings too much! (even if it's The Thrillezs' fault).

